          "text": "{\"relation\":\"REFINED\",\"consensus_summary\":\"Darkness primarily symbolizes moral and spiritual evil—sin, unbelief, ignorance, and alienation from God—in contrast with divine light, while also carrying several context-dependent secondary senses.\",\"book_summary\":\"Darkness signifies disobedient or evil deeds concealed from exposure by the light.\",\"consensus_core_identification\":\"Moral and spiritual evil or sin opposed to God and divine light.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"Sinful disobedience specifically insofar as it is concealed from exposing light.\",\"core_relation\":\"BOOK_NARROWS\",\"extension_relation\":\"BOOK_SUBSET\",\"boundary_disagreement\":\"The book restricts darkness to concealed disobedience and hidden evil deeds. It thereby excludes or leaves uncovered broader consensus cases such as spiritual ignorance, unbelief, alienation from God, Satanic dominion, overt wickedness, death, judgment, suffering, and primordial darkness.\",\"material_contradiction\":\"There is no contradiction at the center: concealed disobedience is a recognizable instance of the consensus category of sin and moral evil. The disagreement concerns scope and defining precision rather than referent replacement.\",\"rationale\":\"The book retains the dominant moral opposition between darkness and light but identifies a narrower subset: wrongdoing that avoids disclosure and reproof. This is a material restriction of the symbol’s extension, not merely different wording, so REFINED is more appropriate than MATCH. It is neither DIVERGENT nor NOVEL because the book’s identification falls squarely within the consensus understanding and is directly anticipated by its primary Johannine basis.\",\"citation_support\":\"STRONG\",\"strongest_objection\":\"Because John 3:19–20 is a central consensus text and explicitly joins darkness, evil deeds, and avoidance of exposure, the book could be read as a concise contextual expression of the standard meaning rather than a competing limitation. Nevertheless, its unqualified glossary definition makes concealment constitutive and is materially narrower than the established broader identification.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}"
        }
